<h2>Relative Time</h2>
<p>Display a server-rendered timestamp as a live-updating "5 minutes ago" style relative time.</p>

<div class="demo-box">
  <p>
    Posted
    <time data-controller="relative-time" datetime="<%= 5.minutes.ago.utc.iso8601 %>">
      <%= 5.minutes.ago.utc.iso8601 %>
    </time>
  </p>

  <p>
    Due
    <time data-controller="relative-time" datetime="<%= 2.days.from_now.utc.iso8601 %>">
      <%= 2.days.from_now.utc.iso8601 %>
    </time>
  </p>

  <p>
    Forced numeric phrasing ("1 day ago" instead of "yesterday"):
    <time
      data-controller="relative-time"
      data-relative-time-numeric-value="always"
      datetime="<%= 1.day.ago.utc.iso8601 %>"
    >
      <%= 1.day.ago.utc.iso8601 %>
    </time>
  </p>

  <p>
    Re-rendering every 5 seconds:
    <time
      data-controller="relative-time"
      data-relative-time-interval-value="5000"
      datetime="<%= 30.seconds.ago.utc.iso8601 %>"
    >
      <%= 30.seconds.ago.utc.iso8601 %>
    </time>
  </p>
</div>

<p>
  On connect, the controller replaces each element's text content with a
  relative description and re-renders it on an interval (one minute by
  default) so it stays current without a page reload. The
  <code>datetime</code> attribute itself is left untouched, so the element
  stays machine-readable, and <code>aria-live="polite"</code> is applied
  automatically so assistive technology announces updates without
  interrupting the user.
</p>
